Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::the_case_fold_ignores_the_case_of_the_name`.

The defect: under the case fold, `folded_class` never asks the bracket expression about the other case of
the name's byte, so `[a]` matches `a` but not `A` while a literal `a` matches both.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` of the match on the name and on the lowercased name.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ fn class_at(pattern: &[u8], open: usize, c: u8) -> (Option<(bool, usize)>, usize
 /// which is both cases hitting the complement. A byte that is not an ASCII letter has no other
 /// case and costs no second pass.
 fn folded_class(pattern: &[u8], open: usize, c: u8, hit: bool) -> (bool, usize) {
-    let other = other_case(c);
+    let other = c;
     if other == c {
         return (hit, 0);
     }
